Florence-2 model weights — not tracked in git (see .gitignore).

The application loads the local vision-language model from:

    models/florence2-large-ft/

Expected contents: a standard Hugging Face model directory (config.json,
model.safetensors, tokenizer / processor files, etc.).

Upstream source
---------------
Microsoft Florence-2 (large, fine-tuned), MIT licensed:

    https://huggingface.co/microsoft/Florence-2-large-ft

The app presents it to the operator as "JIC-AnyScan-VLM-v1"; the weights are
unmodified Florence-2 (see App/run.py, MODEL_NAME / MODEL_DIR).

How to fetch
------------
Using the Hugging Face CLI (pip install -U "huggingface_hub[cli]"):

    huggingface-cli download microsoft/Florence-2-large-ft \
        --local-dir models/florence2-large-ft

Or with git-lfs:

    git lfs install
    git clone https://huggingface.co/microsoft/Florence-2-large-ft \
        models/florence2-large-ft


FastSAM instance-segmentation weights — not tracked in git
==========================================================

The vision pipeline's stage 2 loads FastSAM-x from:

    models/sam-1/FastSAM-x.pt

Expected contents: the single ~140 MB FastSAM-x.pt checkpoint.

Upstream source
---------------
Ultralytics FastSAM (AGPL-3.0 for the code; the weights are the published
FastSAM-x release):

    https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/fast-sam/

How to fetch
------------
Let ultralytics resolve and download the correct release, then move it into place
(version-robust — no pinned URL to rot):

    python -c "from ultralytics import FastSAM; FastSAM('FastSAM-x.pt')"
    mkdir -p models/sam-1 && mv FastSAM-x.pt models/sam-1/

The pipeline resolves this path from Vision/Segmenter.py the same way the
Florence-2 path is resolved (CONST_SEGMENTER_WEIGHTS); override it per run with
Example/Vision/analyze.py --weights.
